## Operator governance handoff

Required approval count, legitimate review identity, strict up-to-date rules and merge
authority remain operator governance outside plan criteria. An independent COMMENT review
does not supply the required approving review. No bypass or new credentials are authorized.
Exact-head CI and independent review remain required even when local implementation is done.

## Out of Scope

- rimraf/development cleanup, TypeDoc/plugin upgrades, edits to npm's bundled dependencies,
  alternative matchers, forced overrides/resolutions, vendor patches, suppressions, ignore
  lists, new exceptions or waivers, and broader vulnerability remediation.
- Skill syntax, APIs, stored shapes, provider behavior, architecture or performance promises.
- Adopting, editing, commenting on or closing unowned Dependabot PR #677.
- Release PRs, `main` promotion, package publication, automatic merge, ruleset changes or
  new identities. No paid provider tests or exploit execution.

## Evidence

### Execution, owner decisions and artifact provenance

Related to WAT-590

Project `llmist`, target-qualified agent `llmist-implement`, repository
`zbigniewsobiecki/llmist`, authorized snapshot base `dev` at
`ba56f209d65c968ebc2a00f4993e46f9d9473c23`. The owner explicitly permits this preserved
base without fetching: newer dev adds only the unrelated 007 documentation spec and its
fragment. Integration with current dev and strict freshness remain operator merge gates.
The supplied parent SHA-256 matches before its completion transition.

Owner decision [WAT-591](https://linear.app/mongrel/issue/WAT-591): Zbigniew approves direct
runtime minimatch `^11` under `BlueOak-1.0.0` instead of ISC on 2026-11-10 at 18:55 UTC,
reaffirmed on 2026-11-11 at 03:12 UTC. Task 1 changes only its license expectation; all
other gates remain unchanged. Baseline 9.0.9 is ISC; fetched upstream artifacts confirm
the Blue Oak Model License 1.0.0 in both manifest and `LICENSE.md`.

Ordinary range resolution selects minimatch **11.0.7**. Full registry metadata, the fetched
tarball and its manifest/types/source are inspected before the accepted dependency edit.
Its SHA-512 matches registry metadata and the final lock:
`sha512-Tnk+M9mPjqKDZlUd77eMSjPjhnlBIa1mABOwetMryIshUwi1YmOBdGFfQnHgn4Z8A66eLT8ENzJrxwYmKfqrZg==`.
Installed ESM source byte-matches that tarball. Engines `20 || >=22` cover Node 22.0.0
and this worker's Node 24.22.2. Both actual artifact branches export the named `minimatch`
function: `dist/esm/index.js` for import and `dist/commonjs/index.js` for require; both
execute an ordinary brace-pattern match in Node. Dependencies are
`@isaacs/nonrecursive-glob-match ^1.1.0` and `brace-expansion ^5.0.12`.

The upstream README describes replacing regular-expression segment matching with the
nonrecursive matcher. Source/types retain default optimization level 1, dot exclusion,
case sensitivity, negation, brace/extglob support and disabled Unicode normalization.
The new segment parser and brace-row merging justify ordinary character-class, escaped
metacharacter, Unicode, comment and level-one optimization cases in addition to the plan
matrix. This is bounded characterization, not exhaustive glob equivalence. No matcher
options or production TypeScript change is applied. The two selection changes below are
explicitly owner-approved; all other preservation requirements remain mandatory.
No speed effect is claimed or benchmarked.

### Baseline and candidate command acceptance

Toolchain: Node 24.22.2, installation npm 10.9.2 at `/usr/local/bin/npm`; release-tool npm
11.21.2 remains separate. Baseline and candidate engine-strict lifecycle-enabled installs
exit 0. Direct Lefthook installation exits 0; executable pre-commit, commit-msg and pre-push
hooks invoke Lefthook. The postinstall `@unblessed/core/dist/data` symlink resolves. The
candidate install preserves the lock hash. Consumer Node `>=22.0.0`, `.nvmrc` 22,
contributor prerequisites, toolchain manifests and hook configuration remain unchanged.

