The reconciliation checker requires every affected installed node/version and a real parent
edge, and deduplicates advisory objects separately from propagated entries. Deliberately
omitting one known row fails; the complete 42-node/40-entry table passes. Manual comparison
of the baseline/candidate inventories confirms all remaining paths, versions, GHSAs and
upstream boundaries are represented, including the actual npm bundle. Total counts alone
do not establish runtime remediation.

### Lifecycle, scope and verification

Targeted typecheck and lint pass after test authoring, after the upgrade and after adding
the two approved regressions. The six final tiers run sequentially on 2026-11-11 from
04:26:53 through 04:28:32 UTC, all exit 0:

| Tier | Observed result |
|---|---|
| `npm run build` | Four package tasks successful |
| `npm run typecheck` | Six tasks successful |
| `npm run lint` | Exit 0; existing warning/info diagnostics remain, no suppression introduced |
| `npm test` | 250 files, 7,069 tests pass |
| `npm run test:coverage` | Same 250 files / 7,069 tests pass; statements 77.12%, branches 78.61%, functions 77.79%, lines 77.41% |
| `npm run test:e2e` | Eleven files pass; 99 tests pass, four opt-in live tests skipped in three files |

`RUN_LIVE_RESEARCH_TESTS` stays unset. The fresh-context `agent-plugins__z:local-review`
gate, round 2, converges against the approved contract and complete delta with no must-fix
finding. The reviewer verifies both baseline failures and candidate selections. Final
lifecycle/documentation edits also undergo completion review before the normal-hook commit.

#### Owner-approved ordinary default matching changes

The independent reviewer checks baseline 9.0.9 and the built candidate through real
`Skill.fromContent` → `SkillRegistry.from` → `findByFilePath` and observes:

| Pattern | File path | Baseline 9.0.9 | Candidate 11.0.7 |
|---|---|---|---|
| `src/!(a)*.ts` | `src/ab.ts` | Unselected | Selected |
| `src/?.ts` | `src/😀.ts` | Unselected | Selected |

An independent in-session Node check also reproduces both results, comparing the installed
baseline matcher against real built candidate skill selection with the same YAML patterns.
These are ordinary default-option inputs, not exploit probes. The registry's unchanged
production delegation exposes the different results directly to users. Positive extglob
alternatives and literal Unicode tests do not cover these changed negative-extglob and
wildcard/code-point semantics.

Owner decision [WAT-609](https://linear.app/mongrel/issue/WAT-609): Zbigniew chooses option
"a" on 2026-11-11 at 04:23 UTC, accepting and documenting exactly these two changes:
`src/!(a)*.ts` now selects `src/ab.ts`, and `src/?.ts` now selects `src/😀.ts`, while 9.0.9
selected neither. Only these two preservation expectations change. The owner explicitly
requires unchanged matcher options, no production-code changes and no accommodation of
any further behavioral difference. The original preservation expectations and assertions
remain intact; two new registry matrix rows pin the newly authorized selections.

Both new regression tests first run against the installed 9.0.9 matcher by temporarily
changing only the registry import in the unfinished tree. Each fails for the intended
assertion: expected `["selected"]`, received `[]`. Restoring the original production import
returns the candidate to green: all 185 tests across the eleven skill files pass. No
temporary mutation remains. The implementation fragment documents both accepted changes.
This addresses the review finding through an explicit contract amendment and regression
coverage, without a silent waiver or a broader relaxation. Parent requirements are not
rewritten; their sole-plan completion is qualified by this recorded owner direction.
Normal hooks, all existing assertions and required CI jobs remain enabled. Only the declared
test files, direct manifest/required lock changes, this plan's lifecycle/evidence, coverage
conclusions, parent completion and one implementation fragment belong to the delta.
CLAUDE.md is untouched by this spec — nothing to audit. No new cross-spec decision record
is needed: the license authorization is feature-scoped and recorded above; global guidance,
README and migration docs do not change; the changelog names both accepted matching changes,
and public APIs, configuration and stored shapes remain intact.

The sole plan reaches `status: done` / `.md.done` after its done-gate. Its only parent
reaches `status: done` / `.md.done`; byte comparison against the pinned source permits only
that status substitution. Coverage links and conclusions follow the completed filenames.
Manual scope review verifies the declared file set, exact five-entry lock delta, only the
direct manifest range, one new implementation fragment, all original registry test lines
preserved and the production registry byte-identical to the base. No shared guidance
or historical evidence is changed. The mechanical done-gate and final scope/link checks
are enforced before committing; no local blocker uses the CI-only handoff.

Exact-head `lint-and-test`, `validate-commits` and `e2e-tests`, then independent review of that
head, remain required after trusted-hook publication. Local review is not the required
approving review. Approval identity, strict freshness and merge authority remain with the
operator; no release, paid-provider test, publication of packages or governance change occurs.

